# Mongo

## Collection naming

Models register with `JXPSchema.model(name, schema)` in `models/*_model.js`. Mongoose pluralizes `name` for the Mongo collection (e.g. `reader` → `readers`, `Label` → `labels`). See [JXP schemas](https://jxp.readthedocs.io/en/latest/schemas/).

Databases: `revengine-dev` (local/docker), `revengine-prod` (production).

## mongodump

**Do not** pass multiple collections in one `-c` (e.g. `-c "labels orders readers"`). That is a single collection name; only the first collection may appear to run.

Use a loop — one collection per invocation:

```bash
DB=revengine-prod
COLLECTIONS="apikeys articles configs customer_values dailyhits devices goals hits interactions jobs labels links logs mailers mailruns mlpredictions orders pipelines quicket_tickets readers refreshtokens reports rfvs saved_charts savedcharts scheduled_reports segments sentmails subscriptions tallies tests tokens usergroups users whitebeardcontents whitebeardcustomers whitebeardnewsletterevents whitebeardnewsletters whitebeardnewsletterstats whitebeardorders whitebeardsubscriptions"

for c in $COLLECTIONS; do
  mongodump --db "$DB" -c "$c"
done
```

With URI: `mongodump --uri="mongodb://localhost:27017/revengine-prod" -c "$c"` inside the loop.

Omit `tests` from `COLLECTIONS` to skip test data. To dump the entire database, omit `-c` and use only `--db` or `--uri`.

